    "q-75282": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the tangent line to the polar curve $r=1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ at $\\theta =\\pi ,$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\theta )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ),\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the equation of the tangent line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\theta )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ),\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P:$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )}{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-2\\cdot 0}{-0-2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P:$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-1 \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi  \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(-1,0).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the tangent:\n\nWe find the equation of the tangent as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (x-(-1)) \\\\ y-0 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (x+1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14215763/assets/7065086643b98b95b5d6face85544f33b00f73614a855fb9846ba68e5d987a33.png)",
