    "q-40691": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$2.3\\overset{―}{43}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The given repeating decimal can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2.3\\overset{―}{43} & =2.343\\,43... \\\\  & =2.3+0.043+0.000\\,43+0.000\\,004\\,3+… \\\\  & =2.3+{{\\frac{43}{1\\,000}+\\frac{43}{100\\,000}+\\frac{43}{10\\,000\\,000}+⋯.}_{⏟}}_{\\text{geometric series}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that we have a geometric series where the first term is ${a}_{1}=\\frac{43}{1\\,000}$ and the common ratio is $\\frac{1}{100}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2.3\\overset{―}{43} & =2.3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2.3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{43}{1\\,000}{(\\frac{1}{100})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2.3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{43\\cdot 100}{1\\,000}{(\\frac{1}{100})}^{n} \\\\  & =2.3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{43}{10}{(\\frac{1}{100})}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
