    "q-96454": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{tanh}^{2}⁡(3x-2)}{3}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1-{tanh}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sech}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =3x-2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{tanh}^{2}⁡(3x-2) & ={sech}^{2}⁡(3x-2) \\\\ {tanh}^{2}⁡(3x-2) & =1-{sech}^{2}⁡(3x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{tanh}^{2}⁡(3x-2)}{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int (1-{sech}^{2}⁡(3x-2))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int 1\\cdot \\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {sech}^{2}⁡(3x-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x-2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
