    "q-103125": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Find the radius of convergence $R$ and interval of convergence $I$ for the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x+5)^{n}}{n(n+1)}\\,.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "To apply the ratio test, we define ${a}_{n}=\\frac{(x+5)^{n}}{n(n+1)}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(x+5)^{n+1}}{(n+1)(n+2)}\\cdot \\frac{n(n+1)}{(x+5)^{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{n(x+5)}{n+2}| \\\\  & =|x+5|{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n}{n+2} \\\\  & =|x+5|{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{(1+\\frac{2}{n})}) \\\\  & =|x+5|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =|x+5|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series converges if $L<1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x+5| & <1 \\\\ -1<x+5 & <1 \\\\ -6<x & <-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the radius of convergence is $R=1,$ and the series converges for any $x$ that lies in the open interval $(-6,-4).$\n\nThe ratio test gives no conclusion about the convergence of the series when $L=1.$ So, when $|x+5|=1,$ we do not know if the series converges. This means that the endpoints $x=-6$ and $x=-4$ need to be investigated separately using another test for convergence.\n\n- When $x=-6$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x+5)^{n}}{n(n+1)} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-6+5)^{n}}{n(n+1)} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}+n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is convergent by the alternating series test.\n\n- When $x=-4$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x+5)^{n}}{n(n+1)} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-4+5)^{n}}{n(n+1)} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{1}^{n}}{{n}^{2}+n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}+n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the above series with  ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}},$\nwe see that the series is convergent by the comparison test.\n\nSo the interval of convergence is $I=[-6,-4].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-103125-a",
